$ python tools/check_action_pins.py --help
# exit=0 duration=0.060s
usage: check_action_pins.py [-h] [--strict] [--root ROOT]

Verify every SHA-pinned GitHub Action resolves upstream.

options:
  -h, --help   show this help message and exit
  --strict     also fail when a pin's trailing version comment (e.g. '#
               v3.2.0') does not match a tag the pinned SHA actually points at
  --root ROOT  repository root to scan (default: this file's repository).
               Present so the fail-closed branches can be exercised against a
               staged tree -- without it the empty-pin-set path could only be
               asserted about, not run, and tests/test_action_pin_checks.py
               was doing exactly that. Every other gate in tools/ takes this
               option.
